<title>USA: Zeneca settles suit for $2.7 mln and costs.</title>
<headline>Zeneca settles suit for $2.7 mln and costs.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zeneca Inc, a unit of Zenca Group Plc, said Thursday it has reached agreement with 48 states, Puerto Rico and the District of Columbia, to pay $2.7 million, plus costs, to the settling states to resolve a dispute over its discontinued stewardship bonus agreements.</p>
<p>The company said it explicitly denies any wrongdoing and has settled with the states without admitting any liability.</p>
</text>
